whole ownership residential products under the Ritz-Carlton Residences brand name, as well as has a license to use the St. Regis brand for specified fractional ownership products. The company also offers exchange network and membership programs, as well as management services to other resorts and lodging properties through its Interval International and Aqua-Aston businesses. In addition, it provides financing for consumer purchases of vacation ownership products; and renting vacation ownership inventory. The company sells its upper upscale tier vacation ownership products under its brands primarily through a network of resort-based sales centers and certain off-site sales locations. Marriott Vacations Worldwide Corporation was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Orlando, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew E. Avril CPA | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $890,109 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $238K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Marriott Vacations Worldwide Co is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.8B market cap on $5.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 11% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The company is burning through $29M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $83.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical se